WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.486
Market Architect brings everything together: evidence, valuation,

2
00:00:05.486 --> 00:00:10.550
risk and clear communication, into a research view you can defend.

3
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.521
Start with a precise question.

4
00:00:14.521 --> 00:00:15.892
Gather evidence.

5
00:00:15.892 --> 00:00:20.349
Turn it into a range of values, not a single number.

6
00:00:20.349 --> 00:00:21.720
Weigh the risks.

7
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:27.034
And state your conclusion together with what you will monitor.

8
00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:31.151
A valuation depends on its assumptions.

9
00:00:31.151 --> 00:00:36.514
For a fictional company with next year’s free cash flow of one hundred crore,

10
00:00:36.514 --> 00:00:39.231
growing at four percent a year forever,

11
00:00:39.231 --> 00:00:45.987
the value is about one thousand six hundred and sixty-seven crore at a ten percent discount rate,

12
00:00:45.987 --> 00:00:51.769
one thousand two hundred and fifty at twelve percent, and one thousand at fourteen.

13
00:00:53.168 --> 00:00:56.524
Write the thesis, the strongest counter-thesis,

14
00:00:56.524 --> 00:01:00.665
and the specific evidence that would invalidate your view.

15
00:01:00.665 --> 00:01:03.878
Then decide in advance what you will monitor.

16
00:01:05.278 --> 00:01:08.180
Risk also lives at the portfolio level.

17
00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:14.728
With thirty percent volatility per share and an average correlation of zero point three,

18
00:01:14.728 --> 00:01:20.235
spreading across twenty shares cuts volatility to about seventeen percent,

19
00:01:20.235 --> 00:01:22.467
but never below about sixteen.

20
00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.327
Correlation sets a floor.

21
00:01:25.727 --> 00:01:31.140
In the course you will build and stress-test a discounted cash-flow model,

22
00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:37.283
measure portfolio risk, validate models, and present an integrated research dossier.

23
00:01:37.283 --> 00:01:43.353
A defensible view states its assumptions, its range, and what would prove it wrong.

24
00:01:43.353 --> 00:01:46.352
This is education, not investment advice.

